From 09eefb07e5b5639481b858b2536a4f72e4ffc7cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 13:32:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Close remaining parity gaps before NNS-python migration

Triage and close the gaps tracked in docs/parity_results.md.

nns_boost cache parity: the previously reported
test_nns_boost_ivs_test_none_matches_r failure was CV-split
seed-sensitivity on an unseeded call. The boosted result is
empirically seed-invariant and matches the committed R cache to
~3.5e-15. Pin the seed in the parity test and add a seed-invariance
regression guard. No tolerance loosened.

NNS.copula discrete + multivariate: generalize nns_copula to the exact
R NNS.copula algorithm. Support continuous=False (discrete) and 2-D
(observations, variables) matrix input for any column count >= 2.
Adopt all four original R fixture values (bivariate continuous/discrete
and three-column continuous/discrete) to 1e-5. Refactor the regression
copula helper to reuse the shared implementation.

PM.matrix naming: add an optional NumPy-first names echo that mirrors
R's data-frame dimname behavior without changing the numeric arrays or
native dispatch. Add a parity test proving names match R while numeric
matrices are byte-for-byte identical.

Plot policy: add docs/plot_parity_policy.md formalizing that
graphics-device artifacts (including Rplots.pdf) are inventoried but
never compared in CI; parity compares returned values only.

Skips: clarify the 11 remaining skips as intentional live-R-only
practical examples, not cache-backed parity gaps.

Update docs/parity_results.md, parity_status.md, parity_plan.md, and
original_tests_adoption.md with the closure summary and final status.

Verified: tests/invariants 314 passed; PYNNS_R_CACHE_ONLY=1 tests/parity
1778 passed, 11 skipped; original copula tests 12 passed; ruff and mypy
clean; python -m build succeeds.
